---
title: P09 Step 6 - optimistic version check on the guard row (no lock; measured on PostgreSQL 16)
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant A as Terminal A - Maya
  participant DB as PostgreSQL: room_booking_guard.version
  participant B as Terminal B - Omar

  A->>DB: BEGIN, SELECT version -> 0 (plain read, no lock)
  A->>DB: overlap check -> 0
  B->>DB: BEGIN, SELECT version -> 0 (nobody waits)
  B->>DB: overlap check -> 0
  B->>DB: UPDATE ... SET version = version + 1 WHERE room = 'R7' AND version = 0 -> 1 row
  B->>DB: INSERT R101, COMMIT
  A->>DB: UPDATE ... WHERE version = 0 -> 0 rows (not an error: a fact)
  A->>DB: ROLLBACK - everything decided so far is stale
  A->>DB: BEGIN again, SELECT version -> 1, overlap check -> 1
  A->>DB: COMMIT - nothing inserted, Maya is told Unavailable
  Note over A,B: Nobody waits, the loser does its work twice. The retry must redo the<br/>check, and needs a limit.
